From 64ca2bd38804131beb1e75bdd933a5fec595f356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:45:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a linux-riscv64 platform

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; python-wheels does not open issues/PRs on third-party repos]

Build the same shared libraries natively on a riscv64 host, in a
Rocky Linux 10 (glibc 2.39) container, the way linux-arm64 is built
natively in a Rocky Linux 8 container. The platform files are the
linux-arm64 ones with the RISC-V triplet, Rust host and -march=rv64gc
baseline swapped in, and Rocky 10's own GCC 14 in place of
gcc-toolset-15. The rv64gc baseline matches what lovell/sharp-libvips'
linux-riscv64 platform uses.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
